Drop lance-linalg's AVX-512 VNNI kernels: they do not compile with this
repo's rustc.

nixpkgs builds rustc against an LLVM whose vpdpwssd.512 / vpdpbusd.512
intrinsic signatures disagree with the declarations stdarch ships in this
Rust release, so the three lance-linalg 11.0.0 kernels that call them fail
with:

  error: intrinsic signature mismatch for `llvm.x86.avx512.vpdpwssd.512`:
  expected signature `<16 x i32> (<16 x i32>, <16 x i32>, <16 x i32>)`,
  found `<16 x i32> (<16 x i32>, <32 x i16>, <32 x i16>)`

Upstream's release binaries come from the rustup toolchain, which bundles the
LLVM those declarations were written for and compiles them fine; this package
takes the repo's rustPlatform, which pins no per-package toolchain.

Only the kernels go: the AVX2 ones stay, the scalar reference and the tests
that compare against it are untouched, so results do not change. What is lost
is the 64-element-per-iteration AVX-512 kernel on CPUs that have VNNI.

Applies to the vendored lance-linalg 11.0.0 (funes pins `lance-linalg
= "=11.0.0"`). Regenerate when that pin moves.

